# Kaggle credentials — never commit
kaggle.json
access_token
.kaggle/
*.env
.env

# The PTCG battle engine and the sample submission are licensed
# "competition use only — do not redistribute or post publicly".
# This repo is public, so they must never be committed.
engine/
submission/
cg/
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*Card*Data*.csv
*Card_ID*List*.pdf
# The sample deck ships with the licensed sample_submission. Our own deck list
# replaces it and can be committed; the vendor sample cannot.
agent/deck.csv

# Competition data / caches
cache/
*.zip
# Exclude data/ contents, not the directory itself — git cannot re-include a
# file whose parent directory is excluded, and the mined summaries are small
# enough to version.
data/*
!data/meta_cards.csv
!data/meta_decks.csv
!data/history_cards.csv
!data/history_archetypes.csv
!data/history_agents.csv
# The fitted margin -> P(win) table the agent ships and reads at run time.
!data/calibration_v2.json
# Same rule for the two C1/C2 tables: the agent ships them in the bundle and
# reads them on every position it scores, so they are versioned with it.
!data/analysis/
data/analysis/*
!data/analysis/trajectory_curves.json
# D47 neural leaf: winning model + fit reports + gate results + attribution
# examples (ptcg/leaf/train.py and scripts/leaf_gates.sh regenerate them;
# the training parquets stay out — 8 GB, rebuilt by ptcg/leaf/build_table.py).
!data/analysis/leaf/
# The v2 ladder autopsy: loss taxonomy over the real ladder games (report +
# machine-readable companion; scripts/autopsy_v2.py regenerates the json).
!data/analysis/LADDER_AUTOPSY_V2.md
!data/analysis/ladder_autopsy_v2.json
# Mono-sprint typing report (scripts/mono_sprint_report.py regenerates the
# tables from runs/mono_sprint/; the narrative sections are hand-written).
!data/analysis/MONO_SPRINT.md
# Stratified leaderboard fitness panel + manifest (D38 amendment; card-id
# lists mined from public replays — same provenance as agent/deck_priors).
!data/panel_lb.json
!data/analysis/PANEL_LB.md
# Ladder-representative weighted panel v3 (D46; scripts/build_panel_v3.py,
# lists from public-replay autopsy — same provenance as panel_lb.json).
!data/panel_ladder_v3.json
!data/analysis/PANEL_V3.md
# Matchup deny-posture spec + its design note: integration surface for the
# agent side (ptcg/matchup_postures.py regenerates the json).
!data/analysis/postures.json
!data/analysis/POSTURES.md
!data/energy_mechanics.json
# Playbook entry 7: the D34 tree leaf. Same rule again — the agent bundles it
# and walks it on every scored position whenever CABT_TREE_LEAF is on, which
# is the one environment variable the refused entry's retest needs.
!data/analysis/tree_leaf.json
# Interaction mining (the D34 salvage): the nomination report and the two
# artifacts its numbers are read from. The features CSV it also produces
# regenerates from local mined data and stays untracked, the
# tree_features.csv rule.
!data/analysis/INTERACTION_MINING.md
!data/analysis/interaction_shap.json
!data/analysis/interaction_screen.json
# Playbook entry 4: the counted opponent reply table. Same rule again — the
# agent ships it in the bundle and reads it on every rollout of their turn.
!data/opponent_policy.json
# Top-5 team profiles: per-team submission trajectories, deck repertoires and
# matchups mined from Meta Kaggle + public replays (report + raw companion).
!data/analysis/TOP5_PROFILE.md
!data/analysis/top5_profile.json

